<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brychan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">5th century</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> · Also known as Brychan Brycheiniog</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brychan is a legendary 5th-century king who gave his name to the Welsh kingdom of Brycheiniog. Medieval genealogies make him the son of an Irish prince and a Welsh princess and credit him with a great many children, a large number of whom were venerated as saints in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wales">Wales</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cornwall">Cornwall</a> and Brittany. He belongs to tradition rather than recorded history.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/brychan.jpg" alt="Brychan" width="229" height="334" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Menter Brycheiniog&amp;amp;Maesyfed · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Brychan_(straightened)_Eglwys_Aberhonddu_(Brecon,_Wales)_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
